---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const base='/equipment/10-08/', manual='https://www.sutter.com/hubfs/WEB%20-%20Manuals/BV-10_OpMan.pdf', photo='https://www.sutter.com/hs-fs/hubfs/WEB%20-%20Product%20Images/BV-10_lg.jpg?height=1483&name=BV-10_lg.jpg&width=2000';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Sutter BV-10-D · documentary model and facet annotation" description="Inspect a stationary documentary model and fit angles on pre-authored fictitious reference drawings. No tip fabrication or operation." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment bv"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/10-08/">← Equipment 10-08</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#bv-evidence">References and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">10-08 · DOCUMENTARY MODEL / FIRST PASS</span><h2>Sutter BV-10-D</h2><p>Inspect the stationary instrument and annotate the angle between two lines in an independent, fictitious reference drawing. This does not modify material or simulate an electrode.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>Stationary instrument</h3><div id="bv-view" aria-label="Orbitable static BV-10-D with cream enclosure, unlit lamp, fixed disk and stereo head"></div><div class="bar"><button data-bv-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-bv-view="detail">Stereo head and stage</button><button data-bv-view="rear">Rear shell</button></div><p id="bv-ready" role="status">Loading metric model…</p><p>Drag to orbit; pinch or scroll to zoom. The teal teaching badge selects a different reference drawing. Every visible machine part is fixed and inactive.</p></section>
<section><h3>Fictitious facet reference</h3><canvas width="700" height="320" id="bv-diagram" aria-label="Two already-authored reference line tracks with optional angular fit overlay"></canvas><label>Reference drawing<select id="bv-fixture"><option value="0">A · 3–4–5 triangle</option><option value="1">B · vertical and diagonal</option></select></label><div class="bar"><button class="primary" id="bv-inspect">Measure drawn angle</button><button id="bv-overlay">Hide fitted lines</button><button id="bv-reset">Reset</button></div><p id="bv-status" aria-live="polite">Choose a drawing, then measure its existing angle.</p><output id="bv-result">No angle annotation yet.</output><button id="bv-export" disabled>Export annotation JSON</button></section></div>
<section id="bv-evidence"><h3>Geometry and evidence</h3><p>The selected BV-10-D has the documented stereo head and no separate readout box. The <a href={photo}>manufacturer front three-quarter photograph</a> and <a href={manual+'#page=1'}>Rev. 3.00 cover</a> show the cream housing, fixed desk footprint and optical head. <a href={manual+'#page=35'}>Rev. 3.00 printed p. 33</a> lists the nominal BV-10 dimensions; they set the scale here, not dimensions of the individual attachments. No separate rear photograph was verified, so the rear is inferred.</p>
<div class="grid"><figure><img width="650" height="420" src={base+'front.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original front rendering of the inactive BV-10-D silhouette"/><figcaption>Original render, not a photo. Compared with Sutter’s cover for enclosure, lamp arm, base and component placement.</figcaption></figure><figure><img width="650" height="420" src={base+'detail.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original close-up of the stereo head and fixed visual hardware"/><figcaption>Original stereo-head close-up. The unpowered silhouettes are proportional estimates and do not represent functional mechanisms.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Reference</th><th>Actual / meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Nominal published scale</td><td>19 × 9 × 8 inches (BV-10 family)</td><td>482.6 × 228.6 mm footprint; 203.2 mm nominal height anchor. Undocumented attachment dimensions inferred.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Independent 3–4–5 geometry</td><td>acos(4/5) = 36.869897646°</td><td>36.869897646° fitted, tolerance 10⁻¹⁰°. Synthetic coordinates only.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Vertical and diagonal geometry</td><td>45°</td><td>45° fitted; line order and rigid display rotation do not change the angle.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Register held-out electrode acceptance</td><td>Before/after tip area and resistance</td><td>Not implemented or run. This release contains no fabrication, electrode model, or resistance estimate.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>The demo takes two authored XY point tracks in millimeters. It fits each by total least squares, finding the dominant covariance direction and measuring orthogonal RMS residual. It reports the acute undirected angle between directions using <code>atan2(|cross|, |dot|)</code>. Coincident and isotropic tracks are rejected because they cannot define a line. The reference is a macro drawing, not a physical specimen, calibrated microscope image, or hardware setting.</p>
<p><a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender generator</a> · <a href={base+'bv10d-static.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'facets.json'}>Authored input fixture</a> · <a href={base+'example-annotation.json'}>Output example</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a>. No real equipment, living material, or headset testing.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/10-08/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.bv{max-width:76rem}.bv .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.1rem}.bv section{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem 0;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}.bv .bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.44rem;margin:.55rem 0}.bv label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.2rem;font-size:.92rem}.bv select,.bv button{font:inherit;color:var(--text);background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.14rem;max-width:100%;min-width:0;min-height:2.4em;padding:.32em .52em}.bv button{cursor:pointer}.bv button:disabled{opacity:.52;cursor:default}.bv .primary{color:white;background:#245350}.bv #bv-view{height:clamp(270px,31vw,435px);background:#d9dddf;touch-action:none}.bv #bv-view :global(canvas){width:100%;height:100%;display:block}.bv #bv-diagram,.bv img{width:100%;height:auto}.bv #bv-result{display:block;white-space:pre-line;margin:.45rem 0;font:1rem monospace}.bv #bv-status.error{color:#a54a34}.bv .scroll{overflow:auto}.bv table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.89rem}.bv td,.bv th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-align:left;padding:.45rem}.bv figure{margin:.8rem 0}@media(max-width:800px){.bv .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
